.N., Larson, S.L., Fabian, G., Granade, S., Bench- and field-scale evaluation of chromium and cadmium extraction by electrokinetics (2004) J Hazard. Mater., 110, pp. 53-62;<br/>Zhou, D.M., Cang, L., Alshawabkeh, A.N., Wang, Y.J., Hao, X.Z., Pilot scale electrokinetic treatment of a Cu contaminated red soil (2006) Chemosphere, 63, pp. 964-971;<br/>Lee, Y.J., Choi, J.H., Lee, H.G., Ha, T.H., Bae, J.H., Pilot-scale study on in situ electrokinetic removal of nitrate from greenhouse soil (2011) Sep. Purif. Technol., 79, pp. 254-263;<br/>Kim, B.K., Park, G.Y., Jeon, E.K., Jung, J.M., Jung, H.B., Ko, S.H., Baek, K., Field application of in situ electrokinetic remediation for As-, Cu-, and Pb-contaminated paddy soil (2013) Water Air Soil Pollut., 224, pp. 1-10;<br/>Rosestolato, D., Bagatin, R., Ferro, S., Electrokinetic remediation of soils polluted by heavy metals (mercury in particular) (2015) Chem. Eng. J., 264, pp. 16-23;<br/>Alshawabkeh, A., Gale, R.J., Ozsu-Acar, E., Bricka, R.M., Optimization of 2-D electrode configuration for electrokinetic remediation (1999) J. Soil Contam., 8, pp. 617-635;<br/>Foust, D.F., Extraction of mercury and mercury compounds from contaminated materials and solutions, US Pat. n. 5,226,545, 1993; Verdonckt, F., Maes, A., Process and apparatus for recovering heavy metals from contaminated materials, Eur. Pat. Appl. n. EP 1,090,695 A1, 2001; Pool, W., Electrically enhanced in situ remediation of contaminated soil, Intern. Appl. n. WO 2005/053866 A1, 2005; Trellu, C., Mousset, E., Pechaud, Y., Huguenot, D., van Hullebusch, E.D., Esposito, G., Oturan, M.A., Removal of hydrophobic organic pollutants from soil washing/flushing solutions: a critical review (2016) J. Hazard. Mater., 306, pp. 149-174;<br/>Rahner, D., Ludwig, G., Röhrs, J., Electrochemically induced reactions in soils – a new approach to the in-situ remediation of contaminated soils. Part 1: the microconductor principle (2002) Electrochim. Acta, 47, pp. 1395-1403;<br/>Bagatin, R., A. 