   abstract = {During the recent years the common agricultural policy aimed to optimizing the technical means used by farms. The realization of these objectives requires a rational use of water resources in agriculture and the Irrigation Advisory Services (IAS) could be new tools for this achievement. In order to express an opinion on the effects expected by the adoption of IAS this survey has involved more than 100 farmers. In general in this study the innovation has been perceived as an opportunity, especially for increase the value of agricultural products and reduction of the management costs. © 2017, SRAC - Societatea Romana Pentru Asigurarea Calitatii. All rights reserved.},
