assics to the Frontiers, , Beijing: The Commercial Press;<br/>Fu, B., Pan, N., Integrated studies of physical geography in China: Review and prospects (2016) Journal of Geographical Sciences, 26 (7), pp. 771-790;<br/>Lu, D., Wang, Z., Feng, Z., Academic debates on Hu Huanyong population line (2016) Geographical Research, 35 (5), pp. 805-824;<br/>(1997) Rediscovering Geography: New Relevance for Science and Society, pp. 109-137. , Washington DC: National Academy Press;<br/>Yao, S., Zhang, P., Yu, C., The theory and practice of new urbanization in China (2014) Scientia Geographica Sinica, 34 (6), pp. 641-647;<br/>Fu, B., Zhang, L., Land-use change and ecosystem services: Concepts, methods and progress (2014) Progress in Geography, 33 (4), pp. 441-446;<br/>Cheng, G., Xiao, H., Fu, B., Advances in synthetic research on the eco-hydrological process of the Heihe River Basin (2014) Advances in Earth Science, 29 (4), pp. 431-437;<br/>Day, T., Core themes in textbook definitions of physical geography (2017) The Canadian Geographer, 61 (1), pp. 28-40},
