 Effect of glyphosate on the microbial activity of two Romanian soils (2010) Communications in Agricultural and Applied Biological Sciences, 75, pp. 167-172;<br/>Tilman, D., Cassman, K.G., Matson, P.A., Naylor, R., Polasky, S., Agricultural sustainability and intensive production practices (2002) Nature, 418, pp. 671-677;<br/>Vance, E.D., Brookes, P.C., Jenkinson, D.S., Microbial biomass measurements in forest soils: The use of the chloroform fumigation-incubation method in strongly acid soils (1987) Soil Biology and Biochemistry, 19, pp. 697-702;<br/>Vasconcellos, R.L.F., Bonfim, J.A., Baretta, D., Cardoso, E.J.B.N., Arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi and glomalin-related soil protein as potential indicators of soil quality in a recuperation gradient of the Atlantic Forest in Brazil (2016) Land Degradation &amp; Development, 27, pp. 325-334;<br/>Zaccheo, P.V.C., Neves, C.S.V.J., Mariano, D.C., Zorzenoni, T.O., Higashibara, L.R., Piccinin, G.G., Okumura, R.S., Green manure in fruticulture: Aspects on soil quality and use in agriculture (2013) African Journal of Agricultural Research, 11, pp. 1469-1474;<br/>Zaller, J.G., Heigl, F., Ruess, L., Grabmaier, A., Glyphosate herbicide affects belowground interactions between earthworms and symbiotic mycorrhizal fungi in a model ecosystem (2014) Scientific Reports, 4, p. 5634},
   title = {Cover cropping system and mulching can shape soil microbial status in fruit orchards},
