   note = {Cited By :37<br/><br/><br/><br/>CODEN: BIRTE<br/><br/><br/><br/>Correspondence Address: Ren, Z.J.; Department of Civil, Environmental, and Architectural Engineering, University of Colorado BoulderUnited States; email: jason.ren@colorado.edu<br/><br/><br/><br/>Export Date: 19 March 2020<br/><br/><br/><br/>References: Baranitharan, E., Khan, M., Prasad, D., Teo, W., Tan, G., Jose, R., Effect of biofilm formation on the performance of microbial fuel cell for the treatment of palm oil mill effluent (2014) Bioprocess Biosyst. Eng.; <br/>Forrestal, C., Xu, P., Jenkins, P.E., Ren, Z.J., Microbial desalination cell with capacitive adsorption for ion migration control (2012) Bioresour. Technol., 120, pp. 332-336;<br/>Forrestal, C., Huang, Z., Ren, Z.J., Percarbonate as a naturally buffering catholyte for microbial fuel cells (2014) Bioresour. Technol., 172, pp. 429-432;<br/>Haeger, A., Forrestal, C., Xu, P., Ren, Z.J., High performance spiral wound microbial fuel cell with hydraulic characterization (2014) Bioresour. Technol., 174, pp. 287-293;<br/>Huggins, T., Wang, H., Kearns, J., Jenkins, P., Ren, Z.J., Biochar as a sustainable electrode material for electricity production in microbial fuel cells (2014) Bioresour. Technol., 157, pp. 114-119;<br/>Janicek, A., Fan, Y., Liu, H., Design of microbial fuel cells for practical application: a review and analysis of scale-up studies (2014) Biofuels, 5, pp. 79-92;<br/>Kim, Y., Hatzell, M.C., Hutchinson, A.J., Logan, B.E., Capturing power at higher voltages from arrays of microbial fuel cells without voltage reversal (2011) Energy Environ. Sci., 4, pp. 4662-4667;<br/>Kivi, I., Anderson, E., Moller, P., Nurk, G., Lust, E., Influence of microstructural parameters of LSC cathodes on the oxygen reduction reaction parameters (2012) J. Electrochem. Soc., 159, pp. 743-750;<br/>Kumar, G., Sarathi, V., Nahm, K., Recent advances and challenges in the anode architecture and their modifications for the applications of microbial fuel 