trasting water regimes (2016) Plant and Soil, 398, pp. 47-57;<br/>Zhang, Y., Yao, Q., Li, J., Hu, Y.L., Growth response and nutrient uptake of Eriobotrya japonica plants inoculated with three isolates of arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi under water stress condition (2014) Journal of Plant Nutrition, 37, pp. 690-703;<br/>Zhao, R.X., Guo, W., Bi, N., Guo, J.Y., Wang, L.X., Zhao, J., Zhang, J., Arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi affect the growth, nutrient uptake and water status of maize (Zea mays L.) grown in two types of coal mine spoils under drought stress (2015) Applied Soil Ecology, 88, pp. 41-49;<br/>Zou, Y.N., Wu, Q.S., Huang, Y.M., Ni, Q.D., He, X.H., Mycorrhizal-mediated lower proline accumulation in Poncirus trifoliata under water deficit derives from the integration of inhibition of proline synthesis with increase of proline degradation (2013) PLoS ONE, 8},
