@article{Sato2009,
   abstract = {The incentive to the use of renewable energies, especially biofuels, replacing the fossil originated ones, became an alternative in application to global warming. Thus, among these distinguishes the biodiesel, mainly from the Jatropha curcas L. The objective of this assay is to present studies about the use of this specie for fuel making, besides agronomical studies made until this moment in view of discuss and confront them. To remark, the information about the cultivation is, in general, deficient and conflictive, on the productive, economical, social, political, environmental and energetic levels. However, their sustainability is still not verified, and the research about the subject is eminent, not only in Brazil but also in other countries.},
