 44 (2), pp. 361-379;<br/>Oke, A.E., Ogunsami, D.R., Ogunlana, S., Establishing a common ground for the use of structural equation modelling for construction related research studies (2012) Construction Economics and Building, 12 (3), pp. 89-94;<br/>Otache, I., Entrepreneurship education and undergraduate students' self-and paid-employment intentions: A conceptual framework (2019) Education+ Training, 61 (1), pp. 46-64;<br/>Pan, Y., Smith, S.C., Sulaiman, M., Agricultural extension and technology adoption for food security: evidence from Uganda (2018) American Journal of Agricultural Economics, 100 (4), pp. 1012-1031;<br/>Rao, G., Transition from Subsistence to Commercialised Agriculture: A Study of Krishna District of Andhra, C 1850-1900 (1985) Economic and Political Weekly, pp. A60-A69;<br/>Ronstadt, R., Contributing editor's feature (1991) Entrepreneurship Theory and Practice, 15 (2), pp. 79-79;<br/>Singh, K., Srivastva, A., Srinivas, K., Singh, S.K., Gupta, H., Entrepreneurship development in agriculture through agro processing centre: a case study of Almora district in NW Himalaya (2007) Agricultural Engineering International: CIGR Journal;<br/>Supe, S., (1969) Factors related to direct degree of response in decision making among farmers., , Ph.. D. Thesis, Indian Agriculture Research Institute, New Delhi;<br/>(2017) Thailand Investment review, , Thailand economy-at-a-glance;<br/>Umali, D.L., Schwartz, L., (1994) Public and private agricultural extension: Beyond traditional frontiers, , The World Bank;<br/>Wanyonyi, N.J., Bwisa, H.M., Factors influencing entrepreneurial behavior among farmers: A Case of Cabbage farmers in Kiminini Ward (2015) International Journal of Technology Enhancements and Emerging Engineering Research, 3 (9), pp. 143-148;<br/>Weitz, R., From peasant to farmer. A revolutionary strategy for development (1971) From peasant to farmer. A revolutionary strategy for development.;<br/>Xue, Y., (2018) The role of the entrepreneurial-oriented unive