@article{NoAuthor201610,
   abstract = {Polygiene, based in Malmö, Sweden, is a global leader in odour control technology. The company was established at the beginning of 2006 as a spin-off from the Perstorp Group. Polygiene develops and sells permanent odour control technology under the brand name Polygiene. The technology was originally developed in the early 2000s in order to provide the surfaces of various plastic materials and industrial flooring with antibacterial properties. During 2007-08, however, the company developed its technology for use on textiles, and today most of its customers are premium clothing brands, particularly in the sports and outdoor sector. Polygiene is a strong believer in environmental sustainability, and it scrutinises its entire supply chain-from sourcing, production and application through to washing and disposal-with the aim of minimising the environmental footprint of its activities. Polygiene odour control technology has been accredited by a number of different organisations and bodies, including bluesign and Oeko-Tex. Also, a product treated with Polygiene odour control technology does not need to be washed by the user as often as a non-treated product and this saves water, energy, time and money, as well as improving the lifespan of the product. Polygiene's sales have increased every year since the company's establishment in 2006. Indeed, over the nine-year period between 2006 and 2015, sales grew by an average of 56.2% per annum. Furthermore, the company expects sales to continue to grow rapidly in the coming years as opportunities arise for expansion into new market sectors and for greater market penetration in the sports and outdoor, lifestyle, and home furnishings sectors. Such opportunities are being aided by a number of advantageous macro and consumer trends.},
   issn = {14776456},
