   abstract = {Canadian Tire Corporation (CTC) has acquired Helly Hansen and its related businesses, The North Face has launched a retail programme called The North Face Renewed, and Unifi has developed new branding for its range of performance fibres and yarns. SOEX and I:Collect have collaborated in the opening of the first footwear recycling plant which can process all types of footwear, and Royal DSM is expanding its capacity for producing Dyneema ultrahigh molecular weight polyethylene (UHMWPE) fibre and Dyneema UD composite unidirectional laminate in order to meet an increase in demand. Aquafil and Genomatica have collaborated to form an initiative called Project EFFECTIVE in order to encourage the production of more environmentally sustainable fibres and plastics, and Lenzing will invest Euro100 mn in improving the environmental sustainability of its production operations. Polygiene has entered into an exclusive distribution agreement with Prebona under which Polygiene has been granted the right to distribute Prebona's OdorControl technology, and HeiQ has entered into a partnership with Concept III in order to strengthen its sales and support its brand partners in North America. Meanwhile, Directa Plus and Arvind have entered into an exclusive collaboration agreement relating to the development of performance denim fabrics. © Textiles Intelligence Limited 2018.},
