   abstract = {Increases in quarterly sales have been reported by Under Armour (up by 36%), Columbia Sportswear (up by 22%) and Unifi (up by 5%), and in annual sales by Nike (up by 10%). However, falls in quarterly sales have been reported by Quiksilver (down by 10%), Puma (down by 7%), Adidas (down by 6%) and Perry Ellis International (down by 2%). Hunter will open its first stand-alone flagship store in London, UK, and Under Armour will open its largest Under Armour Brand House to date in Chicago, USA. Bestseller will acquire M and M Direct from TA Associates, and Columbia Sportswear will acquire PrAna from its majority shareholder. Meanwhile, Milliken & Company has acquired Westex, and Patagonia has invested in CO2 Nexus via its $20 Million & Change venture capital fund. Ohmatex has entered into an agreement with Danfoss PolyPower relating to the supply of PolyPower stretch sensors for use in wearable applications, while Perry Ellis International has entered into a licensing agreement with Parigi Group relating to the manufacture of children's sportswear and swimwear and has entered into a licensing agreement with the Flyers Group relating to the manufacture of children's apparel under the Original Penguin brand. A subsidiary of PVH Corp has entered into a licensing agreement with Vandale Industries relating to its Warner's and Olga brands, and Downlite has entered into an agreement with Nikwax relating to the supply of Nikwax Hydrophobic Down (NHD) to manufacturers of outdoor apparel and sleeping bags. TenCate Protective Fabrics has entered into an agreement to supply the Zaanstreek-Waterland fire brigade with flame resistant (FR) firefighter turnout gear, and has won a contract to supply Arkema with 60,000 m of its Tecasafe Plus XL-9300 fabric for use in the manufacture of workwear. Archroma has increased the prices of its textile dyes in response to the enforcement of environmental regulations. The Zero Discharge of Hazardous Chemicals (ZDHC) Group has released its Manufacturing Restricted Substances List (MRSL), Adidas has released its latest Sustainability Progress Report and announced a new plan to eliminate the use of hazardous chemicals from its products and supply chain by 2020, and Nike has released its latest Sustainable Business Performance Summary. Meanwhile, a Greenpeace study claims that football merchandise produced by Nike, Puma and Adidas contains hazardous chemicals. Unifi has announced plans to expand its Repreve Recyling Center as part of its strategy to focus on developing the Repreve brand while Solvay has obtained a European patent from the European Patent Office which protects the use of its Emana yarn. Meanwhile, Messe München has decided to stage the ISPO (International Trade Fair for Sports Equipment and Fashion) Beijing trade fair twice a year starting in 2015 in order to increase its coverage of the Chinese sportswear market. © Textiles Intelligence Limited 2014.},
