   abstract = {<p> The two species of <italic>Typha</italic> common in the southeastern United States, <italic>T. latifolia</italic> and <italic>T. domingensis</italic> differ substantially in their tolerance to deep water. The objective of this study was to examine the morphology and biomass allocation of these two species to determine if they have similar phenotypic responses to water depth. Replicate monocultures of the two species were established at a range of water depths in an artificial pond and allowed to grow for three growing seasons. At the end of the experiment, subsamples were harvested for determination of plant morphology as well as above‐ and belowground biomass. </p>},
